```
- `CreateEscapedChildKey` at line 338 escapes segment separators in the child value
- `CreateChildKey` at line 345 creates a child without escaping (assumes value is pre-validated)

#### 4. Escape Character Handling

**UnescapedCharCount (`HierarchicalKey.cs:122-141`)**
```csharp
private static int UnescapedCharCount(ReadOnlySpan<char> value)
{
    var isEscaped = false;
    var result = 0;
    foreach (var c in value)
    {
        if (!isEscaped && c == SegmentSeparator)
        {
            ++result;
            isEscaped = false;
        }

        if (c == EscapeCharacter)
        {
            isEscaped = !isEscaped;
        }
    }

    return result;
}
```
Counts unescaped '/' characters by tracking escape state. When backslash is encountered at line 134, the `isEscaped` flag toggles (allowing '\\\\' to escape the backslash itself). Unescaped '/' increments counter at line 129.

**Escape (`HierarchicalKey.cs:96-120`)**
```csharp
private static string Escape(ReadOnlySpan<char> value, int unescapedChars)
{
    var resultArray = ArrayPool<char>.Shared.Rent(value.Length + unescapedChars);
    var isEscaped = false;
    var insertions = 0;
    for (var i = 0; i < value.Length; i++)
    {
        var c = value[i];
        if (!isEscaped && c == SegmentSeparator)
        {
            resultArray[i + insertions] = EscapeCharacter;
            ++insertions;
            isEscaped = false;
        }

        if (c == EscapeCharacter)
        {
            isEscaped = !isEscaped;
        }

        resultArray[i + insertions] = c;
    }

    return new string(resultArray.AsSpan(0, value.Length + unescapedChars));
}
```
Rents a buffer from `ArrayPool<char>.Shared` at line 98 sized for the original length plus the number of escape characters needed. Iterates through the value at line 101, inserting '\\' before unescaped '/' characters at lines 104-106. Returns new string at line 119.

#### 5. Validation (`HierarchicalKey.cs:193-243`)

**IsSegmentationValid**
```csharp
private static bool IsSegmentationValid(ReadOnlySpan<char> value)
{
    var isEscaped = false;
    var segmentLength = 0;
    foreach (var c in value)
    {
        ++segmentLength;

        if (isEscaped && c != SegmentSeparator && c != EscapeCharacter)
        {
            // The only characters which can be escaped are the escape character itself 
            // and the segment separator.
            return false;
        }

        if (c == EscapeCharacter)
        {
            // The escape character is allowed and can be used to escape itself.
            isEscaped = !isEscaped;
        }
        else if (c == SegmentSeparator)
        {
            // Check if this is the start of a new segment.
            if (!isEscaped)
            {
                if (segmentLength <= 1)
                {
                    // Empty segments are not allowed
                    return false;
                }

                segmentLength = 0;
            }

            isEscaped = false;
        }
    }

    // The sequence must not end with an incomplete escape sequence.
    if (isEscaped)
    {
        return false;
    }

    // Empty segments are not valid
    if (segmentLength == 0)
    {
        return false;
    }

    return true;
}
```
Validates three rules:
1. Lines 201-204: Only '/' and '\\' can be escaped
2. Lines 217-223: Empty segments (consecutive '//') are invalid
3. Lines 231-234: String cannot end with incomplete escape sequence (trailing '\\')
4. Lines 237-240: Final segment cannot be empty

#### 6. Relationship Methods

**IsParentOf (`HierarchicalKey.cs:257-288`)**
```csharp
public bool IsParentOf(HierarchicalKey? other)
{
    if (other is null) return false;
    var left = GetEnumerator();
    var right = other.GetEnumerator();
    while (true)
    {
        var leftValid = left.MoveNext();
        var rightValid = right.MoveNext();
        if (!leftValid && !rightValid)
        {
            // Completed enumeration, both keys are equal and there is no 
            // parent/child relationship between them.
            return false;
        }
        else if (leftValid && !rightValid)
        {
            // The left key is longer than the right key, so it is not a prefix of it.
            return false;
        }
        else if (!leftValid && rightValid)
        {
            // The right key is longer than the left key, and all common components 
            // are equal, so the left is the parent of the right if the right has 
            // one more segment.
            return !right.MoveNext();
        }
        else if (!left.Current.SequenceEqual(right.Current))
        {
            // Some segment is not equal and therefore neither is a prefix of the other.
            return false;
        }
    }
}
```
Uses segment enumerators at lines 260-261 to compare segments. Returns true only if:
- All segments of `this` match the corresponding segments of `other` (line 282)
- `this` has exactly one fewer segment than `other` (line 280 - the `!right.MoveNext()` check ensures only one more segment exists)

**IsChildOf (`HierarchicalKey.cs:250`)**
